{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/58027-specific-differences-between-the-cwod-and-our-own","id":58027,"title":"Specific differences between the cWoD and our own","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-26T04:46:30-08:00","id":58027,"title":"Specific differences between the cWoD and our own","content":"If an average human was moved from our world to the World of Darkness, what specific differences to every day life would they notice? What institutions would look different?<br /> <br /> For example, it\u2019s mentioned in a few places that the Catholic Church is larger and more powerful in the WoD than in our world. I\u2019m assuming this person is oblivious to the supernatural. I also don\u2019t mean the general \u2018more corruption, more conflict on the streets\u2019 that you see in the introductions in the WoD chapters of books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u200b<span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\">Dante \u201cOwns-All-the-Books\u201d Laughing-Coyote<br /> <a href=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/91390940/Werewolf%20the%20Apocalypse%20Reference.xlsx\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf (and Human) Reference Excel Spreadsheet</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/clouddrive/share?s=VoD6R2UDSGwijaft3H4kbM\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img593/9752/w20supporterhiddengarou.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img546/6111/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1765-rderekp","name":"rderekp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T04:55:44-08:00","id":58029,"title":"","content":"Pentex and its subsidiaries replace many of the massive corporate entities we know today. I think the most notable shifts their would be their control of the oil industry and them being a major figure (publisher, most likely) in the video games industry (almost certainly standing in for the pure evil of EA, probably? I kid, I kid.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T09:50:27-08:00","id":58144,"title":"","content":"There was the Apophis pipeline mentioned in Rage Across Egypt. It's entirely fictional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T10:03:21-08:00","id":58156,"title":"","content":"From what I could always tell, the buildings would be different too. The openings always specifically mentioned more gargoyles and medieval type decorations on even modern buildings. People seem more religious, and I would imagine large religious organizations are more powerful. Pentex is a big one, and probably would qualify as a &quot;megacorporation&quot;. I wonder of other corporations are more monolitic and diversified than they are now. I think the attitude towards violence and poverty would be different, as in fewer/less effective social programs, more random street crime, etc. I know that in the real world RICO played a big part in ending the heyday of organized crime, but I bet in the WoD it never passed. the Mafia should be more like the movie versions of the Mob, and the other organized crime syndicates are larger and more dangerous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T10:20:14-08:00","id":58164,"title":"","content":"Oh, one other thing; explicitly stated to be more overpopulated than our world. I don't know if that means 8 billion or 11 billion, but more than what we have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T11:29:18-08:00","id":58200,"title":"","content":"If you're going to do this, remember to phrase your sentences/paragraphs like <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Dark_Alliance:_Vancouver\" target=\"_blank\">DA: V</a> did, &quot;In the real world...., in the world of Darkness...&quot;. Cause I remember how annoying that was in that book. You don't need to tell me two different versions of a place, DA:V.<br /> <br /> <u><b>To Atamajakki:</b></u><br /> Tellus was created before the evil of EA was full known (1992/1993). You can figure out which company it was supposed to be at the time in the way you say the name (Tell-us). Also, said company was well known for the type of advertising it did. The time of creation, way they describe Tellus' ads, and the way you say the name, <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=c2duS4RsEwI\" target=\"_blank\">well...</a><br /> By 1999, this company was on it's last console, but nobody at the time and even White Wolf knew that. So I think Onyx Path would have to go either a couple of ways on this:<br /> 1. Tellus no longer makes any consoles, it has gone totally into software. It is either no longer the major player it once was or see &quot;2.&quot;.<br /> 2. Change the comparison from what it used to be to EA, so it doesn't lose it's influence.<br /> <br /> Also, OP should change a lot of the old 90'ish view on video games to be much more current. Like the use of <a href=\"http://gamasutra.com/blogs/BarbaraJones/20130418/190804/The_Playstation_War_Conflict_Minerals_and_Video_Game_Manufacturing.php\" target=\"_blank\">conflict minerals</a>, influencing <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tropes_vs._Women_in_Video_Games\" target=\"_blank\">toxic views</a> (Read the harassment section) in the gamers that play their games, paying/bribing game journalists and let's players to promote/lie about their games (<a href=\"http://arstechnica.com/gaming/2014/01/electronic-arts-also-paying-youtubers-to-promote-games/\" target=\"_blank\">EA was caught doing this recently...</a>), among other things rather than just the old early 90's standby of, &quot;Hee hee, video games make you violent!&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","user":"Laughing Hyena","date":". 01-26-2014, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T20:52:31-08:00","id":58494,"title":"","content":"I shudder to imagine what the WoD version of <a href=\"http://fatuglyorslutty.com/\" target=\"_blank\">online console chats</a> look like.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChewyGranola</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/58027-specific-differences-between-the-cwod-and-our-own?p=58156#post58156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I could always tell, the buildings would be different too. The openings always specifically mentioned more gargoyles and medieval type decorations on even modern buildings. People seem more religious, and I would imagine large religious organizations are more powerful. Pentex is a big one, and probably would qualify as a &quot;megacorporation&quot;. I wonder of other corporations are more monolitic and diversified than they are now. I think the attitude towards violence and poverty would be different, as in fewer/less effective social programs, more random street crime, etc. I know that in the real world RICO played a big part in ending the heyday of organized crime, but I bet in the WoD it never passed. the Mafia should be more like the movie versions of the Mob, and the other organized crime syndicates are larger and more dangerous.</div> </div> </div> </div>RICO was actually addressed in Hunters Hunted 2, at least in as much as to mention that it failed to gut them like it did in the real world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 01-26-2014, 11:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T21:24:21-08:00","id":58503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/58027-specific-differences-between-the-cwod-and-our-own?p=58164#post58164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, one other thing; explicitly stated to be more overpopulated than our world. I don't know if that means 8 billion or 11 billion, but more than what we have.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd make this specifically mean overpopulation in Cities not so much the world in comparison to ours.<br /> <br /> Other thing you would notice is that people's general view on things is more hardened than ours I.E less catastrophe aid funding, more and worse conditioned homeless shelters, run down social services and public hospitals as a rule, more underfunded schools etc. More obvious corruption and neglect among governmental officials and there's no part in cities where you don't have the feeling of threat, making people dead bolt their doors thrice every night even at the 'better' neighbourhoods and suburbia unless fenced and guarded by armed guards Ala Brazil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1700-blue-fox","name":"Blue Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1700_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T08:34:37-08:00","id":58730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blue Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/58027-specific-differences-between-the-cwod-and-our-own?p=58503#post58503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd make this specifically mean overpopulation in Cities not so much the world in comparison to ours.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ditto. IMO, there's not necessarily more people in the world, but most people are crowded in cities. I picture rural areas full of ghost towns and small, closed communities. The wilderness is more dangerous in the WoD, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/355-romanov","name":"romanov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar355_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T09:01:53-08:00","id":58758,"title":"","content":"Yup, people running for the (supposed) safety of the cities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T17:53:28-08:00","id":59330,"title":"","content":"The couple times it passed through Utah, the cWoD seemed to think it was all Dunes and Cactus. Much of the state <i>is</i> desert, but not that <i>specific type</i> of desert. In fact, it's the specific type of desert that movie people seem to think should be Texas (which is not at all like any part of Texas I've ever seen).<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the treatment of Hawaii in &quot;Immortal Eyes: Shadows on the Hill&quot; wasn't half bad. Some of the geography was a bit abstract, but a lot of the cool stuff in there, they actually had to <i>under-sell</i> to make it believable enough for a <i>Changeling</i> book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please add signature.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/615-the-hanged-man","name":"The Hanged Man","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T20:00:39-08:00","id":59409,"title":"","content":"For the most part my group and I use the WoD as is, at least in the particular line we're playing. We'll make small tweaks to things like the population of supernatural races but largely things are largely as presented in the books.<br /> <br /> Though there has been one recent game where we changed things, our first (and to date only) W20 game. My players get interested in playing as White Howlers in the modern day. So we cooked up a world where the BSD did emerge from the Howlers but it didn't destroy them. Some of the ideas we threw around were actually pretty interesting and I have to admit I'm eagerly awaiting the WH TB to mine for ideas and come up with a more complete outline of the modern day White Howlers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T22:52:31-08:00","id":59535,"title":"","content":"Vampire the Masquerade, the roleplaying game would probably not exist. Meaning White Wolf didn't have the success to publish the other World of Darkness games, Exalted and whatnot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/657-skafte","name":"skafte","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar657_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T23:38:26-08:00","id":59566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>skafte</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/58027-specific-differences-between-the-cwod-and-our-own?p=59535#post59535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampire the Masquerade, the roleplaying game would probably not exist. Meaning White Wolf didn't have the success to publish the other World of Darkness games, Exalted and whatnot.</div> </div> </div> </div> Black Dog produces the popular World of Shadow line of roleplaying games. There's equivalents for most of the gamelines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T23:45:05-08:00","id":59570,"title":"","content":"Yeah, LARPers, and roleplayers in general, are probably a wilder bunch in the WoD - the Black Dog games are supposed to give Wyrm taint to the players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1506-lubricus","name":"Lubricus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T07:30:56-08:00","id":59792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lubricus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/58027-specific-differences-between-the-cwod-and-our-own?p=59570#post59570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, LARPers, and roleplayers in general, are probably a wilder bunch in the WoD - the Black Dog games are supposed to give Wyrm taint to the players.</div> </div> </div> </div> There's the absolutely wonderful picture (is it from Pentex: Subsidiaries?) where a group of high school students are playing Warlock: the Pretension. The Storyteller has a mummified cat hanging from his waist, the girl is driving a sacrificial knife through her palm, one kid is blowing his brains out with a handgun (that reminds me; would firearms be more common in the World of Darkness?), and they're all laughing their asses off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T07:41:35-08:00","id":59801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/58027-specific-differences-between-the-cwod-and-our-own?p=59792#post59792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There's the absolutely wonderful picture (is it from Pentex: Subsidiaries?) where a group of high school students are playing Warlock: the Pretension. The Storyteller has a mummified cat hanging from his waist, the girl is driving a sacrificial knife through her palm, one kid is blowing his brains out with a handgun (that reminds me; would firearms be more common in the World of Darkness?), and they're all laughing their asses off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Man, I loved <i>that</i> book. Yes, I do suppose guns would be more common in the WoD. Perhaps the Brady bill was never passed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/355-romanov","name":"romanov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar355_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T11:11:41-08:00","id":59968,"title":"","content":"One thing that would be different would be the body count.<br /> <br /> The world is crowded and overpopulated, yeah, but people keep... <i>disappearing</i>. Sometimes they just vanish, completely, as if they were never there. Sometimes they show up drained of blood in a &quot;cult killing&quot;. Gang murders claim dozens and virtually no-one bats an eyelid. Sometimes wild animal attacks occur right in the middle of a city... it's a weird world, isn't it?<br /> <br /> Thing is, all these things happen in our world, all the time. We all just ignore them. It's easier not to think about how cheap life can be sometimes. Isn't it? It's just... for most of us, these tragedies will be a distant tale, something that happened to someone we know's friend's family's neighbour.<br /> <br /> In the WoD on the other hand... this is a part of everyday life. Most people have a childhood friend who falls in with the wrong people and dies in mysterious circumstances. Nearly everyone with an extended family will have a relative who one day just... vanishes completely. No-one in the press seems to want to know, of course, but then this isn't really news, is it?<br /> <br /> Probably best to buy some more Pentex-branded booze and try to forget about it. Wait a minute... what was that banging noise in the cellar?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/698-chalicier","name":"chalicier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T13:03:31-08:00","id":60066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>chalicier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/58027-specific-differences-between-the-cwod-and-our-own?p=59968#post59968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing that would be different would be the body count.<br /> <br /> The world is crowded and overpopulated, yeah, but people keep... <i>disappearing</i>. Sometimes they just vanish, completely, as if they were never there. Sometimes they show up drained of blood in a &quot;cult killing&quot;. Gang murders claim dozens and virtually no-one bats an eyelid. Sometimes wild animal attacks occur right in the middle of a city... it's a weird world, isn't it?<br /> <br /> Thing is, all these things happen in our world, all the time. We all just ignore them. It's easier not to think about how cheap life can be sometimes. Isn't it? It's just... for most of us, these tragedies will be a distant tale, something that happened to someone we know's friend's family's neighbour.<br /> <br /> In the WoD on the other hand... this is a part of everyday life. Most people have a childhood friend who falls in with the wrong people and dies in mysterious circumstances. Nearly everyone with an extended family will have a relative who one day just... vanishes completely. No-one in the press seems to want to know, of course, but then this isn't really news, is it?<br /> <br /> Probably best to buy some more <b>Pentex-branded booze</b> and try to forget about it. Wait a minute... what was that banging noise in the cellar?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pentex isn't a brand. King, however, is.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T22:50:19-08:00","id":60496,"title":"","content":"Absurdly, some of the wild animal populations in WoD would be better off than in the real world. It is stated, for instance, that the Get of Fenris has a healthy line of wolf Kinfolk. In the real world, the wolves supposed to be of that stock are extinct in Germany and Denmark, and there are hardly any left in Scandinavia. And the ones that are left are mixed with the Finno-Russian wolves, so there would be no Pure Breed for Get of Fenris if they were real.<br /> <br /> TL/DR: In the World of Darkness, the Northern European wolf stock would have to be a lot stronger and purer than in the real world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1506-lubricus","name":"Lubricus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T08:32:41-08:00","id":61562,"title":"","content":"I believe the standard police force carry guns in the UK in the World of Darkness, where they don't in real life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2149-isvan","name":"Isvan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T19:19:20-08:00","id":61931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/58027-specific-differences-between-the-cwod-and-our-own?p=59792#post59792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There's the absolutely wonderful picture (is it from Pentex: Subsidiaries?) where a group of high school students are playing Warlock: the Pretension. The Storyteller has a mummified cat hanging from his waist, the girl is driving a sacrificial knife through her palm, one kid is blowing his brains out with a handgun (that reminds me; would firearms be more common in the World of Darkness?), and they're all laughing their asses off.</div> </div> </div> </div>The file is a tad too big for this forum. <a href=\"http://imgur.com/oZucv7q\" target=\"_blank\">http://imgur.com/oZucv7q</a><br /> <br /> Gotta love how delightfully depraved World of Darkness can be. Who else wants to run a Warlock: The Pretension game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>\u201cAnd those who were seen dancing were thought to be insane by those who could not hear the music.\u201d - Friedrich Nietzsche</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/812-datura","name":"Datura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar812_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T23:01:17-08:00","id":62010,"title":"","content":"I've always wanted to try a Human: The Protagonist game myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1506-lubricus","name":"Lubricus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T23:38:57-08:00","id":62023,"title":"","content":"Cities in general seem to be &quot;awake&quot; and active a lot more into the night than most are in reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}